<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iron smelting</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as iron production</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iron smelting is the extraction of iron from ore by heating it in a furnace. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> was a notable centre of iron production, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meroe">Meroë</a> often associated with large-scale smelting. In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> produced iron on a large scale for tools and weapons.</p></div>
